Synchronous spin integrators (fix nve/spin/sib and fix nve/spin/pc)
===================================================================

These inputs integrate the spin and lattice dynamics of fcc cobalt with the
fixes that advance all spins together, every spin seeing the magnetic field
of the same configuration:

  in.spin.sib   semi-implicit midpoint method at constant energy.
                f_integ[4] reports the average number of magnetic field
                evaluations per timestep.  etotal includes the Zeeman energy
                through fix_modify prec energy yes.

  in.spin.pc    predictor-corrector method with a spin bath at 300 K.  The
                transverse damping, temperature and random seed come from
                fix langevin/spin; the lattice is not thermostatted.

Both inputs require the SPIN and MANYBODY packages and use the Co potential
of the cobalt_fcc example.  Run them from this directory:

  lmp -in in.spin.sib
  lmp -in in.spin.pc

The constant-energy run does not depend on the number of MPI processes.  In
the run with the spin bath each process draws its own random numbers, so the
logs for 1 and 4 processes differ.
